  "article_opening": "Nvidia introduces revenue-sharing model for AI cloud financing\nNvidia has launched a revenue-sharing financing model aimed at AI cloud providers, facilitating access to its computing infrastructure. This initiative is designed to support startups and enterprises in scaling AI operations.\nNvidia launches a revenue-sharing financing model for AI cloud providers.\nThe model aims to facilitate access to large-scale AI compute for startups and enterprises.\nSharon AI and Firmus are early adopters of th",
  "passage": "…ts, there is a growing need for computing supply that can scale with usage while maintaining flexibility in payment structures during the shift from pilot projects to full deployment.\nNvidia highlighted the needs of model builders, inference providers, and enterprises requiring immediate cloud access for various AI-related tasks. The company also pointed to AI-native businesses such as Baseten, Fireworks AI, and Together AI as examples of where demand is heading.\nThese entities depend on reliable access to accelerated computing as customer usage increases, often requiring more adaptable commercial arrangements than traditional data center buildouts or fixed infrastructure commitments allow.\nFor Nvidia, this model not only creates a recurring income stream tied to the usage of supported cloud capacity but also deepens its involvement in the AI cloud market as competition intensifies among providers aiming to serve developers, digital-native companies, and established enterprises.\nSharon AI's co-founder and CEO, James Manning, described the agreement as a milestone for the company's plans, stating, \"This strategic collaboration with NVIDIA marks a pivotal moment in Sharon AI's mission to deliver sovereign, large-scale AI compute infrastructure.\"\nFirmus co-CEO Tim Rosenfield emphasized the importance of infrastructure access for globally competitive AI businesses, noting, \"AI-native companies need access to scalable, energy- and cost-efficient compute infrastructure to compete globally.\"\nHe added that the Firmus AI cloud is building a NVIDIA DS…",
